    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I’m really hearing how heavy that is, and it makes sense that it feels like the hurt has no end—when the world constantly makes you feel wrong, exhaustion can turn into hopelessness. But you’re not the struggle; the struggle is something happening *to* you, and that distinction matters, even when it’s hard to feel. You don’t have to find the \"version of life\" that works all at once—you just have to survive the next hour, and then the next. Existing as yourself in a hostile world is exhausting, but your existence isn’t the problem; the world is. Please don’t carry that alone. If the thought of not existing is there, even as a \"way out,\" that’s a signal to talk to someone right now—988 in the U.S. or your local emergency line. You reaching out here tells me some part of you still wants to be heard, and that part deserves to keep going.",
